WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.380
Previously on The O.C.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.840
Oh my God, Caitlin Cooper?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.760
So how long have you been in love with my sister?

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.480
I don't have feelings for Johnny.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.660
Last one in!

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.040
Caitlin!

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.580
I could really go for a drink.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.280
You read my mind.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.520
Actually, I was hoping that you might have dinner with me sometime.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.700
Neil, I would love to.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.800
You disrespected me.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.160
And the company I'm trying to build.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.300
A guy from Brown, he didn't say that they couldn't take more than once to.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.380
Well, this might be the year.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:21.800
That's right.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.500
Hey baby, have you seen my lucky tie?

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.230
I got it dry cleaned.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.050
Oh, you're an angel.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:35.690
Big day?

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.720
Well, I got to sign some papers, make a few calls, build a hospital.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.130
Building a hospital? Wow.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.010
Well, Caleb deserves most of the credit.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.850
I just inherited the project.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:45.950
So who's paying for?

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.040
The board of the Newport Laguna Medical Center.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.980
They commissioned a proposal from us and from a firm in Brea, and today we're both presenting.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.240
And they're going to pick you.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.100
Well, now that I got my lucky tie.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:58.800
Hey.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.560
Oh, hi.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.720
Are you okay? You seemed a little distracted last night.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.660
Uh, yeah. No, I'm fine.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.790
I don't think that convinced anyone.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.190
I was leaving school yesterday, and Mrs. Rushfield said that some brown rep called

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.260
and wants to interview me on Sunday.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.030
That's great. Why didn't you say anything?

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.740
I don't know. I guess it just needed to sink in.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.000
Did Summer get her interview?

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.830
I forgot to ask, actually. I was just kind of spinning.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.690
Well, you want me to help you out and maybe ask you a few questions?

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:29.970
Yeah.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.650
Yeah, listen, Matt's waiting for me right now, but when I get back, let's talk, we'll practice, whatever you need.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.850
Yeah, gotta go.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.090
I better go, too. Julie and I have a meeting with a new client.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.230
I am so proud of this.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:47.870
Sure you're all right, man?

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.080
Yeah, it's just kind of weird.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:57.250
There I am, and I'm all ready to go, and I got my watch set to East Coast time, and then I get this interview, and it just kind of hit me.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.780
I'm leaving Newport.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:01:59.980
So you're happy?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.840
Second thoughts dude. I plan my first escape on an etch-a-sketch. This is my dream. It's just I don't know now

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.320
It's real. Well, why don't you talk to summer about it? I mean, I'm sure she's freaking out a little bit, too

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:29.840
No, I'm fine. Seriously. This is just my process fair enough. You're pouring coffee in her cereal you poured a hard

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.440
knew you.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.740
Hi, Sam.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.080
An interview with the brown guy Mrs. Rushfield just told me, and that you got one too.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.560
Oh yeah, that's great.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:17.220
Great?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.450
Mrs. Rushfield said they only interview people that they're serious about.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.030
This, like, totally increases our chances of getting in together.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.350
Show some excitement.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:25.490
No, it's amazing.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.910
It's just, are you feeling any anxiety at all about this?

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:29.610
About what?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.720
About leaving Newport and your friends and family

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.640
and going somewhere completely new in September?

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.020
Yeah, honestly, I was.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:37.420
Really?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.980
But then I talked to Colonel Flint.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.700
Who's Colonel Flint?

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.880
He's my boot camp instructor.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:41.740
He's a former Delta.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.560
He says you can either ride change or change rides you.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.590
And also, there's no room in the trenches of life

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:47.610
for whiny little babies.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:47.990
Ah.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.090
Want to see my war phase?

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.530
Oh, that's not messy, sir.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.250
I gotta go.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.490
But it's not September.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.430
Freshman orientation starts August 25th.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:55.240
Oh.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:57.200
Bye.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:57.670
Bye.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:07.890
Situated as it is, the hospital will provide ready access to Newport's affluent and less affluent neighborhoods, servicing the whole community.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.780
More detailed budgets and schedules are in your folders, along with copies of the permits that we pulled.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.310
We know you have another proposal to hear today.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.990
You should know. We're ready to start any time. Just give us the green light.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.990
Well, speaking for all of us, you two have done a great job.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.840
I only wish Caleb could have been here.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.180
Thanks, Bill. This project was close to his heart.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.460
He did have one, as it turns out.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.980
We'll contact you as soon as we...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:44.600
made our decision. Now we wait. What? I took a look at Bray Group's plan this morning. I didn't

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.650
want to tell you because I didn't want to spook you before the presentation. So? It's good. Better

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:55.460
than ours? They're both excellent. But the Bray Group has been whining and dining Bill Merriam

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.880
and the board for months. I mean, dinner, concerts, cruises. Well, we offered him bagels.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.420
they came in i'm worried that we've handicapped ourselves when i got into this i said i wouldn't do

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:10.670
business by applying people with meals and gifts and i respect that i do but what it could all come

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:16.000
down to is who bill merriam likes more well hopefully he'll appreciate the fact that we

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:24.510
appeal to his intelligence and not to his taste for pino here's a picture with caitlin

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:29.440
but what's wrong with this horse that's china she has alopecia

